<title>USA: Seagate Technology may issue $750 mln 3-part debt.</title>
<headline>Seagate Technology may issue $750 mln 3-part debt.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-02-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Seagate Technology Inc is expected to sell $750 million in new corporate debt via a three-tranche deal, syndicate sources said on Monday.</p>
<p>The Baa3/BBB rated deal is expected to consist of a seven-year issue, 10-year issue, and a 40-year tranche, puttable in the twelfth year, sources said.</p>
<p>Morgan Stanley &amp; Co Inc is expected to act as lead underwriter for the offering, they added.</p>
<p>(( -- Nancy Leinfuss, 212-859-1675 ))</p>
